Package: escrow-branding
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Escrow OS Team <team@escrow-os.invalid>
Depends: escrow (= @VERSION@), escrow-shims (= @VERSION@)
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Description: Escrow OS identity: name, login banner, wallpaper, dark theme, logo
 Turns an Ubuntu install into Escrow OS: os-release (NAME, PRETTY_NAME,
 VARIANT_ID=escrow; ID stays "ubuntu" so apt and PPAs keep working),
 lsb-release description, /etc/issue, a message of the day showing escrow
 sessions, the GRUB menu name, a default wallpaper and dark theme (GNOME and
 Xfce) and a logo.
 The original files are kept with dpkg-divert and restored on removal.
 Escrow OS is based on Ubuntu and is not affiliated with Canonical.
